# Transfer-integrity manifest for the offline model artifact.
#
# Generate it on the controlled packaging machine, beside the final GGUF:
#
#   cd deploy/on-prem/models
#   sha256sum reconcileai-recon-3b-q4_k_m.gguf > SHA256SUMS
#
# Rename this template to SHA256SUMS only after replacing the placeholder below.
#
# ── What this file does and does not prove ───────────────────────────────────
# It proves the shipped bytes match what the packaging machine wrote — i.e. the
# media survived the journey. It does NOT prove the artifact is the approved one:
# it travels alongside the GGUF, so anyone able to substitute the model can
# regenerate this manifest to match their substitute.
#
# Authenticity comes from RECON_MODEL_SHA256 in .env.onprem, which the operator
# takes from the signed release record over a DIFFERENT path than this media.
# `model-init` checks both, and the application does not start unless both pass.
# Do not put the approved digest in this file — that would defeat the separation.
REPLACE_WITH_SHA256  reconcileai-recon-3b-q4_k_m.gguf
